Installing PSRCHIVE
===================

Prerequisites
-------------

Required:
  - C++11 compiler (g++ >= 4.8 or clang++ >= 3.3)
  - Fortran compiler (gfortran)
  - FFT library: FFTW3 (recommended), Intel MKL, or Intel IPP
  - GNU autotools: autoconf >= 2.69, automake, libtool
  - pkg-config

Optional:
  - CFITSIO    — PSRFITS file format support
  - TEMPO2     — pulsar timing predictor library
  - PGPLOT     — plotting support
  - GSL        — GNU Scientific Library (statistical routines)
  - readline   — command-line editing in psrsh
  - SWIG + Python dev headers — Python bindings (requires --enable-shared)

On Debian/Ubuntu:
  apt-get install autoconf automake libtool g++ gfortran make pkg-config \
      libfftw3-dev libgsl-dev libreadline-dev

On Arch Linux:
  pacman -S gcc-fortran fftw gsl readline

Basic Build
-----------

  git submodule update --init     # Initialize epsic math library
  ./bootstrap
  ./configure --prefix=/usr/local
  make -j$(nproc)
  make install

Configure Options
-----------------

Build scope:
  --enable-lean         Disable MEAL, Polarimetry, Timing, RFIMitigation,
                        and Plotting modules. Produces a smaller build but
                        is insufficient for DSPSR (which needs Faraday.h
                        from Polarimetry).

Library type:
  --enable-shared       Build shared libraries (.so). Required for Python/SWIG
                        bindings. Default is static libraries only.

Developer options:
  --enable-debug        Keep debugging symbols (-g) in compiled objects.
                        Without this flag, -g is stripped from compiler flags
                        to reduce binary size.
  --enable-werror       Treat all compiler warnings as errors (-Werror).
                        Used in CI to prevent introduction of new warnings.
                        Not recommended for end users as different compiler
                        versions may produce different warnings.

Dependency paths:
  --with-fftw3-dir=DIR        FFTW3 installation prefix
  --with-cfitsio-dir=DIR      CFITSIO installation prefix
  --with-tempo2-dir=DIR       TEMPO2 installation prefix
  --with-pgplot-dir=DIR       PGPLOT installation prefix
  --with-gsl-dir=DIR          GSL installation prefix
  --with-readline-dir=DIR     readline installation prefix

Python Bindings
---------------

  ./configure --prefix=/usr/local --enable-shared
  make -j$(nproc)
  make install
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib
  python3 -c "import psrchive"

Running Tests
-------------

  make check

Tests are self-contained and generate synthetic data internally.
No external test data files are required.
